      "rule": "Panels of torchis (clay and chopped straw over riven laths) on early work, not exceeding about 0.6 m clear width; from the 17th century, brick nogging laid in herringbone or a chequer of red and vitrified black. Torchis and brick nogging belong to different centuries and must not be mixed on one elevation (soft constraint c05).",
